From e1765703d379cca66bea664ae1873e7182a3ad0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds-bootstrap <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:22:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Lobby placement new: use the builtin size_t for the first
 parameter

The four small lobby translation units each define a placement new for the
lobby containers:

  lobby_channel_map_insert_node.cpp:7, lobby_chat_split_string.cpp:5,
  lobby_event_deque_capacity.cpp:7, lobby_user_id_set_copy_nodes.cpp:9

with `inline void *operator new(unsigned long, void *p)`. GCC requires the
first parameter to be the builtin size_t, which is `unsigned int` on i386 and
ARM, so each is rejected with "'operator new' takes type 'size_t'
('unsigned int') as first parameter". MWCC's DS size_t is unsigned long.

Under SDK_PORT_3DS LOBBY_SIZE_T expands to __SIZE_TYPE__; under #else it stays
unsigned long, which is the original token, so the DS preprocessed text is
unchanged. gcc-10 -E -P without SDK_PORT_3DS: byte-identical for all four
files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/lobby/lobby_channel_map_insert_node.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 src/lobby/lobby_chat_split_string.cpp       | 10 +++++++++-
 src/lobby/lobby_event_deque_capacity.cpp    | 10 +++++++++-
 src/lobby/lobby_user_id_set_copy_nodes.cpp  | 10 +++++++++-
 4 files changed, 36 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/lobby/lobby_channel_map_insert_node.cpp b/src/lobby/lobby_channel_map_insert_node.cpp
index 1e34162..a66c16c 100644
--- a/src/lobby/lobby_channel_map_insert_node.cpp
+++ b/src/lobby/lobby_channel_map_insert_node.cpp
@@ -4,7 +4,15 @@
 
 #include "lobby_mem.h"
 
-inline void *operator new(unsigned long, void *p) {
+#if defined(__cplusplus) && defined(SDK_PORT_3DS)
+// GCC requires the first parameter of operator new to be the builtin size_t
+// (unsigned int on i386/ARM), not unsigned long.
+#define LOBBY_SIZE_T __SIZE_TYPE__
+#else
+#define LOBBY_SIZE_T unsigned long
+#endif
+
+inline void *operator new(LOBBY_SIZE_T, void *p) {
     return p;
 }
 
